  "learningBlocks": [
    {
      "id": "l19-b1",
      "type": "concept",
      "title": "Passive form does not always mean passive action",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "Deponent verbs use passive-looking morphology but normally have active meaning. This is a lexical property of the verb: sequitur means 'he follows', not 'he is followed'.",
        "fr": "Les verbes déponents utilisent une morphologie d'apparence passive mais ont normalement un sens actif. C'est une propriété lexicale du verbe : sequitur signifie « il suit », non « il est suivi »."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l19-b2",
      "type": "connection",
      "title": "Lesson 16 already prepared this",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "patior, nascor and morior already showed that participial/passive-looking forms can have active meaning. Lesson 19 turns that preview into a general reading category.",
        "fr": "patior, nascor et morior ont déjà montré que des formes d'apparence passive peuvent avoir un sens actif. La leçon 19 transforme cet aperçu en catégorie générale de lecture."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l19-b3",
      "type": "authentic-example",
      "title": "miserere nobis",
      "sourceId": "mr1962-agnus-miserere-l19",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "miserere is a command: 'have mercy'. Its form resembles passive morphology, but its meaning is active. nobis remains the pronoun/case anchor.",
        "fr": "miserere est un ordre : « ayez pitié ». Sa forme ressemble au passif, mais son sens est actif. nobis reste le repère pronominal et casuel."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "mr1962-agnus-miserere-l19",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l19-b4",
      "type": "authentic-example",
      "title": "Confiteor Deo",
      "sourceId": "mr1962-confiteor-opening-l19",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "confiteor means 'I confess / acknowledge'. The first-person ending -or looks passive, but the lexical meaning is active. Deo marks the person to whom the confession is made.",
        "fr": "confiteor signifie « je confesse / reconnais ». La terminaison -or ressemble au passif, mais le sens lexical est actif. Deo marque celui à qui la confession est faite."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "mr1962-confiteor-opening-l19",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l19-b5",
      "type": "pronoun",
      "title": "Deponents keep their own case government",
      "sourceId": "vulg-jn8-12-l19",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "sequitur me takes accusative me. loquor tecum uses the ablative pronoun inside tecum. Do not assume a deponent needs a 'passive' case pattern; learn its syntax like any other verb.",
        "fr": "sequitur me prend l'accusatif me. loquor tecum emploie le pronom à l'ablatif dans tecum. Un déponent ne crée pas un régime « passif » : sa syntaxe s'apprend comme celle de tout autre verbe."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "vulg-jn8-12-l19",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l19-b6",
      "type": "retrieval",
      "title": "Read morphology, then check lexical voice",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "When a form looks passive, first identify the lemma. If the lemma is deponent, read active meaning; if not, continue with the passive analysis learned earlier. This prevents both over- and under-calling passives.",
        "fr": "Lorsqu'une forme paraît passive, identifiez d'abord le lemme. Si le lemme est déponent, lisez un sens actif ; sinon, poursuivez l'analyse passive déjà apprise. Cela évite les deux types d'erreur."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    }
  ],
